"I'm approving PKT-0096. The oracle meets the goal, the contract and the budget, and I changed no files.\n\n**Goal:**\n- **What runs:** `web-apps-documenteditor.sh` builds both sides, original (`external/web-apps.base`) and new (`external/web-apps`). It runs Chromium against the Document Server, swapping in each side's own `app.js`, `code.js`, `app.css` and locale files. It checks that each side's bundle was actually loaded.\n- **What a case covers:** each of 4 cases (docx ×2, txt, rtf) has two users editing at once. User A edits through the UI and user B makes remote edits. A then saves as DOCX, converts to TXT, and the saved file is reopened.\n- **What it compares:** the document after co-editing, what A and B each sent, the visible editor screen, the reopened document as shown and as laid out, and the converted text. It also prints one timing line per case for both sides.\n- **Supporting pieces:** differences listed in the `.intended` file are let through. Builds are cached by content under `$THESEUS_CACHE_DIR`, with no webpack cache shared between builds (as `baseline.md` requires). It also checks that the scripted edits actually appear in the document, so a run where nothing happened can't pass.\n\n**Contract:**\n- Nothing changed in `external/web-apps`: the diff and working tree are both empty.\n- New files are only under `.theseus/oracle/differential`, plus the packet and `friction.jsonl` updates.\n- The diff is 6 files and about 320 lines, within the budget of 8 files and 1500 lines.\n\n**TEP-0004 checks:**\n- The Executor log is filled in.\n- No follow-ups were asked for, and there is no `.theseus/spawn/`.\n- The log's \"surprise\" is about the environment (both sides are the same commit), not a behavior of the code, so it doesn't need a test.\n- The race in the reopened layout read was fixed by waiting until two reads agree, not by adding it to the `.intended` file. That is the right call, since both sides run the same code.\n\n**Weak spots, none blocking. Worth follow-up packets:**\n1. **Never seen to catch a difference.** Both sides are the same commit (d238e526), so we only know the oracle gives the same result on identical code. Nothing shows it can detect a deliberate change yet; a test that plants a known change on purpose would prove it.\n2. **The reopened-layout wait can give up silently.** It polls up to 40 times; if the layout never settles, it keeps the last read without saying so. A timeout should fail or print a warning.\n3. **One value is computed but never compared.** `savedBytes` is never checked. The saved document is only judged through the reopened document and its screen image, which is acceptable.\n4. **Some changes are deliberately not checked.** The status-bar save message and the co-editor presence box are filtered out because their timing varies, so a change in either would be missed.\n5. **Conversion is checked to TXT only.**\n\nVERDICT: APPROVE oracle covers open/local+remote edits/save/reopen/convert with an intended-differences list, timing lines and cached builds; web-apps code untouched; flaky layout read fixed rather than listed as intended","ttft_ms":7014,"type":"result","duration_ms":40913,"uuid":"582ef5c0-3944-4d45-bc01-f5214e38c531","ttft_stream_ms":5732,"time_to_request_ms":326,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":5,"system_prompt":196,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":13,"input_attachments":24,"input_hooks":3,"conversation_append":1,"transcript_persist":9,"tool_pool_refresh":0,"init_message":9,"init_frame_send":3,"engine_pickup":2,"loop_entry":4,"message_prep":1,"model_config_wait":1,"autocompact":2,"request_announcements":13,"query_setup":6,"auto_mode_context_wait":7,"model_gates":0,"tool_schema_build":16,"message_normalization":3,"client_creation":2,"request_build":6},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index":0,"time_to_request_loop_lag_ms":91,"time_to_request_cpu_ms":152,"time_to_request_major_faults":11,"process_rss_mib_turn_start":207,"process_anon_mib_turn_st